       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. It can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and the effects can last a long time because amlodipine has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours.\n\nTypical adult dosing for hypertension or angina is 2.5 to 5 mg once daily to start, titrated to a maximum of 10 mg once daily.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily (standard starting dose)\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily (maximum dose)\n- Another dose, or a different drug?\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, please tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd suggest confirming with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
